{%- comment -%}
  One catalogue card, rendered on demand for the wishlist page through the
  Section Rendering API:

      /products/<handle>?section_id=mts-wish-card

  Why this exists: the wishlist page used to pre-render the catalogue and hide
  every card except the saved ones. Liquid caps `collection.products` at 50, so
  81 of the store's 131 products could be hearted and then never appear on the
  wishlist — the header badge counted them, the page could not show them.

  Fetching per handle removes that cap, ships ~50 fewer cards of markup on every
  wishlist visit, and — because a dead handle answers 404 — gives the theme a
  reliable way to prune saves whose product has since been deleted or renamed.

  The card names the handle it is for, and renders nothing at all when there is
  no product. That matters: asking for a handle that no longer exists does NOT
  give you a 404 here — Shopify answers 200 and renders this section against an
  empty product, which would otherwise mount a blank card. The wrapper is the
  theme's proof that a real product came back; no wrapper, or the wrong handle
  in it, means the save is dead and mts-theme.js prunes it.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if product.handle != blank -%}
  <div data-mts-wish-card="{{ product.handle }}">
    {% render 'mts-product-card', product: product, index: 0 %}
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{ "name": "Wishlist card" }
{% endschema %}
